  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Amtec has $283M in federal contract obligations in FY26 to date. Amtec won 15 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $18.9M. Obligations are down 29.5% year over year. Year-to-year obligations show variability: FY21 totaled $248M, FY22 totaled $70.4M, FY23 totaled $138M, FY24 totaled $513M, FY25 totaled $401M, and FY26 to date totaled $283M. The mix of award count and average award size indicates Amtec is winning relatively few, larger awards so far this fiscal year. The FY24 peak at $513M and the FY25 total at $401M frame the current-year decline. Stakeholders tracking Amtec should note the fiscal volatility across FY21 through FY26 and the current-year drop in obligations relative to the prior year.",
